  "placementWhy": "Guess, see unverified. Scale from the 1500 ft bar (417 px, 1.096 m/px), north up (decorative compass rose); one point, Cenote Verde, put 250 m (the map's distance) west of highway 307 near the golf course's north access road. The map's highway runs at 22 deg, the real 307 at 29-30 deg here: the drawn road is schematic or the map is rotated about 7 deg; not corrected. Check: the database's Aktun Chen point (Gerrard) lands about 400 m west of Cenote Dos Lados, west of the Tren Maya corridor, where a small dark opening shows in the canopy - possibly a cenote of the system not drawn, or a sign that the map belongs further west. Reviewed on the satellite by the user (2026-10-02) and accepted: no longer unverified (it was: No cenote of the map has a reliable position: the database has none for the map's cenotes (Media Luna, La Dune, Verde, Kep/Kop, Plus, Iglesias, Murd have no coordinates; Ventana and Dos Lados aren't in it) and its only point, Aktun Chen (Gerrard 2015), is a cenote the map doesn't name. No pool of th).",
